  "2026-10-27T02:46:18.309Z","harness:codex","Native reproduction: executable lookup succeeds, but /bin/sh reports absent shebang interpreter with exit126 and the original bad-interpreter diagnostic on this host. The real linked regression failed as assertion_failure before this change (negative log retained privately), then passed after the fix. POSIX shells reporting named not-found/127 use the same bounded-header proof; Windows resolution remains separate. Linux execve documents ENOENT for a missing script interpreter: https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/execve.2.html. The classifier reads at most256 header bytes with nonblocking open, closes the handle, declines incomplete/ambiguous or unavailable evidence, and never reruns the user command. Real executed scripts spoofing both127 and126 diagnostics remain assertions. Focused110 tests pass, including platform controls; focused exact module coverage is100/100/100/100 (42statements,45branches,6functions,37lines), typecheck and focused lint pass."
